al chows in W (e.g., W2-W3-W4 if you draw W4) or B (B3 pair). Also, discarding W9 reduces terminals, which can help if aiming for All Simples later (though you have honors). Alternatively, J2 is a single honor, but dragons are valuable for Dragon Pung (2 pts) if you get a pung, but with only one, it's speculative. F4 is North (prevailing wind), so discarding it might be risky if you draw more later, but you only have one. Given tile counts: W9 has 2 left unshown, B9 has 4 left, J2 has 1 left, F4 has 4 left. W9 is less connected to your hand. So discard W9 to tidy hand.\n\nAnswer: Play W9"}
